# Append-at-top logs: never let a merge silently DROP rows.
#
# These files are written the same way (newest row at the top of a markdown
# table), so two branches that both record work produce overlapping inserts at
# the same line. Git reports that as a conflict, and the natural resolutions
# ("take ours" / "take theirs") discard the other side's rows with nothing left
# behind to notice.
#
# `merge=union` is git's built-in driver: it keeps BOTH sides' lines instead of
# raising a conflict. For an append-only log that is the correct semantic: a row
# is a fact that happened, and two branches recording different facts is not a
# disagreement to resolve.
#
# Tradeoff: union resolves without a conflict marker, so the result is not
# automatically ordered, and a prose edit made on both branches is duplicated
# rather than merged. Duplicated prose is visible on the next read; a dropped row
# is not. After any merge that touches these files, re-sort rows newest-first and
# check that the row count is the full union.
docs/INTAKE_LOG.md  merge=union
docs/TRACE_LOG.md   merge=union
docs/TEST_MATRIX.md merge=union
